hook: PostToolUse Completed
codex
One issue is emerging: the pre-send reload prevents a worker that starts after a sweep from sending, but it does not serialize the check with the actual Schwab call. That leaves room for duplicate jobs or a pause between check and send.
codex
**Findings**
- High: late IDs after `not_placed` are only handled when the caller reloads the attempt first. The real worker path passes stale `@attempt` into `record_submitted!` at [place.rb:24](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/submission/place.rb:24), while `record_submitted!` decides `late = attempt.not_placed?` from that object at [order_proposal.rb:153](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/order_proposal.rb:153). Sequence: worker enters Schwab call with pending attempt; sweep moves row to `submission_unknown`; reconcile marks attempt `not_placed`; Schwab finally returns an ID; stale attempt makes `late` false; transition from `submission_failed` to `submitted` is rejected and swallowed by `Place#record` at [place.rb:49](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/submission/place.rb:49). The working order is then left on a failed row. Fix: reload and lock the attempt/status inside `record_submitted!` before computing `late`, and add a spec through `Submission::Place.call`, not a direct `attempt.reload` call like [place_spec.rb:99](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/spec/models/submission/place_spec.rb:99).

- High: duplicate place workers can still send the same proposal twice. Two workers can both pass the unlocked `@proposal.reload.submitting?` check at [place.rb:21](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/submission/place.rb:21), both call Schwab at [place.rb:23](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/submission/place.rb:23), and only afterward does the row-lock transition reject the second answer at [order_proposal.rb:227](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/order_proposal.rb:227). By then the duplicate order has already been sent. Fix: serialize `Place#call` per proposal/attempt with an advisory lock or durable send lease that covers check/send/record, with the second worker rechecking state after acquiring it.

- High: a late no-ID maybe-sent answer after `not_placed` still leaves a working order unlinked. Sequence: worker passes [place.rb:21](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/submission/place.rb:21), sweep/reconcile records `not_placed` via [order_proposal.rb:181](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/order_proposal.rb:181), then Schwab accepted the order but the client raises `UnknownOutcome`; `record_unknown!` only allows `submitting` at [order_proposal.rb:165](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/order_proposal.rb:165), so `Place#record` swallows it. Later sync will not link it because `ProposalLink` only links submitted/filled/cancelled rows with `broker_order_id` at [proposal_link.rb:17](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/orders/proposal_link.rb:17), and reconcile exits unless the proposal is `submission_unknown` at [reconcile_job.rb:15](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/jobs/submission/reconcile_job.rb:15). Fix: either prevent sweep/reconcile from finalizing while any worker can still send, or allow a late maybe-sent answer from `submission_failed`/`not_placed` to reopen `submission_unknown` and enqueue reconcile.

**Confirmed**
The other stated fixes are present: post-sweep worker skip, 4xx from `submission_unknown` to final failed, ignored illegal answers audited/reported, per-row sweep rescue, stricter matcher fields/shape, scale-out realized P&L, and `pending_new_positions(except:)`.

I did not run tests; this was a read-only review.
